main='''<main id="main"><div class="atlas-breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Overview</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><a href="/evidence/">Evidence</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span aria-current="page">Measured-window quadrature</span></div><div class="page-intro"><div class="eyebrow">21 October 2026 · Local quadrature 0.1</div><h1>Measured samples only.<br>A visible transfer cost.</h1><p class="lede">A fixed weighted least-squares quadrature estimator removes assumed padding and gives an explicit conditional error budget. Its chosen window passes two of six synthetic cases.</p></div><aside class="callout"><strong>Derived conditional / Numerical synthetic · Physical promotion 0</strong><p>Independent review pending. Development — no registry entry. No experimental rerun, action estimate or empirical phase certificate. The previous 0/891 result and EXIT-03 HOLD remain intact.</p></aside><div class="actions"><a class="button secondary" href="/sources/local-quadrature-v0.1/THEOREM.md">Read theorem and proof ↗</a><a class="text-link" href="/sources/local-quadrature-v0.1/REPORT.md">Full benchmark report</a></div><section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-label">01</div><div><h2>A local error interface.</h2><p>The estimator fits cosine, negative sine and a constant baseline in a fixed 2049-sample Hann-weighted window. Its complex coefficient preserves quadrature phase. Every valid output uses measured samples only, with no whole-record demeaning, extension or taper division.</p><p>For independently justified envelope variation L and input uncertainty ε, complex error is bounded in exact arithmetic by d = H₁L + H₀ε. The numerical kernel gives H₀≈2.000000000043 and H₁≈0.000311801908507 seconds. Formal deployment needs numerical enclosures and calibrated source/input bounds.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Valid outputs</th><td>14136 per 16184-sample record</td></tr><tr><th>Window radius / availability delay</th><td>1024 samples / 524.288 microseconds</td></tr><tr><th>Constant phasor and baseline controls</th><td>Maximum numerical error below 2.23×10⁻¹³ V</td></tr><tr><th>Synthetic recovery gates</th><td>2 / 6 passed</td></tr></tbody></table><a class="text-link" href="/sources/local-quadrature-v0.1/KERNEL.csv">Fixed complex kernel ↓</a></div></section><section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-label">02</div><div><h2>Locality does not imply broadband recovery.</h2><p>The exact carrier and a 44.65 Hz offset pass. Smooth amplitude/phase modulation, turn-on, narrow pulse and omitted-sideband full-state recovery fail. The pulse relative RMS error is about 0.549; its fast envelope is strongly smoothed.</p><p>The explicit transfer law includes both main response and conjugate-image leakage. At a 600 Hz offset the main gain is about 0.7694; at 1000 Hz it is about 0.4637. These sampled responses are not a certified continuous passband. No post-result tuning or transfer correction is applied.</p><a class="text-link" href="/sources/local-quadrature-v0.1/RESULTS.json">Transfer and control results →</a><a class="text-link" href="/sources/local-quadrature-v0.1/METRICS.csv">Six-case metrics ↓</a></div></section><section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-label">03</div><div><h2>Freeze the source class before redesign.</h2><p>Next specify envelope bandwidth or regularity, noise, gain/skew bounds, allowed delay, passband distortion and image rejection. Then test whether one fixed local kernel can satisfy the joint budget using a continuous-frequency certificate.</p><p>The theorem supplies a conditional measurement interface. Source regularity, full energy, absolute native support, timing calibration and action normalization remain open.</p><a class="text-link" href="/sources/local-quadrature-v0.1/CONTRACT.json">Frozen estimator contract →</a><a class="text-link" href="/sources/local-quadrature-v0.1/verify.py">Reproduction code ↓</a><a class="text-link" href="/evidence/boundary-benchmark/">Preserved boundary comparison →</a></div></section></main>'''
